{#
    The new/edit form body shared by Activity Types, Escorts, Projects, Users
    and Volunteers: every widget, a Save button, a Cancel link. Those five
    screens differ only in where Cancel goes, which is why they were five
    byte-identical partials before this component existed.

    Activities deliberately don't use it — templates/activity/_form.html.twig
    carries its own usage-event Stimulus wiring.

    `formAttr` is the second and only other difference: Projects pass `{}`
    because ProjectFormType sets the form's attributes itself.

    `sections` (optional) groups the fields into the same emoji-headed cards
    as the entity's show page, so switching from view to edit keeps the
    reader's bearings: a list of {key, emoji, title, fields}, `key` becoming
    the card's id so the show page can deep-link to it. A field the form
    lacks is skipped; one no section lists still renders, after the cards.
    Text areas and checkbox lists span the card's full width.
#}
{% props
    form,
    cancelUrl,
    formAttr = {class: 'max-w-lg'},
    sections = []
%}

{{ form_start(form, {attr: formAttr}) }}
    {% if sections is empty %}
        {{ form_widget(form) }}
    {% else %}
        {% for section in sections %}
            <div id="{{ section.key }}" class="mb-6 scroll-mt-4 rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4">
                <h2 class="mb-3 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-slate-500"><span aria-hidden="true">{{ section.emoji }}</span> {{ section.title }}</h2>
                <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-x-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
                    {% for name in section.fields|filter(name => form.children[name] is defined) %}
                        {% set field = form.children[name] %}
                        {% set wide = 'textarea' in field.vars.block_prefixes or (field.vars.expanded ?? false) %}
                        {{ form_row(field, {row_attr: wide ? {class: 'sm:col-span-2'} : {}}) }}
                    {% endfor %}
                </div>
            </div>
        {% endfor %}
        {{ form_rest(form) }}
    {% endif %}

    <div class="{{ sections is empty ? 'flex items-center gap-3' : 'sticky bottom-0 flex items-center gap-3 border-t border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/95 py-3' }}">
        <button
            type="submit"
            class="rounded-md bg-brand-600 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium text-white hover:bg-brand-700"
        >
            Save
        </button>
        <a href="{{ cancelUrl }}" class="text-sm text-slate-600 hover:underline">Cancel</a>
    </div>
{{ form_end(form) }}
